    "image_with_usp_dFJKGH": {
      "type": "image-with-usp",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_V7bGRi": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Facing the Food Miles Question",
            "heading_flourish": false,
            "heading_underline": "pistachio"
          }
        },
        "usp_P3aU4P": {
          "type": "usp",
          "settings": {
            "usp_heading": "",
            "text": "<h4><strong>Do Food Miles Matter?</strong></h4><p>How can a wine be considered sustainable if it’s travelled from New Zealand? It’s an obvious question. Wouldn’t it be better came from somewhere nearer to the UK?</p>"
          }
        },
        "usp_Jrhhie": {
          "type": "usp",
          "settings": {
            "usp_heading": "",
            "text": "<h4> Well, 'Yes' and 'No' </h4><p>‘Yes’, if the only measure of environmental impact were emissions from transport, and ‘no’, if all the other factors which contribute to a complex process from grape to glass are taken into account.</p>"
          }
        },
        "usp_f8BJVh": {
          "type": "usp",
          "settings": {
            "usp_heading": "",
            "text": "<h4><strong>World Class Wine Production</strong></h4><p>And that’s where New Zealand wine production is the best in the world. Particularly their focused efforts on efficient water use, zero waste to landfill, enhancing the health of soils and regenerative agriculture.</p>"
          }
        },
        "usp_XbTG6X": {
          "type": "usp",
          "settings": {
            "usp_heading": "",
            "text": "<h4>Net Zero by 2050</h4><p>The recent launch of <a href=\"https://www.nzwine.com/en/sustainability/roadmap-to-net-zero/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.nzwine.com/en/sustainability/roadmap-to-net-zero/\">Roadmap to Net Zero</a> (carbon neutral) by 2050 is a testament to their work (once it arrives in the UK it’s up to us).  </p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_V7bGRi",
